<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Dholpur State</h1><p class="st-meta">1806 CE – 1948 CE · capital Dholpur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Jat-ruled state on the Chambal, created in 1806 when the British gave Dholpur to the Rana of Gohad.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Jat Ranas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gohad">Gohad</a> had held lands near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gwalior-state">Gwalior</a> in the 18th century. In 1806 the British returned Gohad and Gwalior to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scindias">Scindias</a> and compensated Rana <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirat-singh-of-dholpur">Kirat Singh</a> with Dholpur, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-bari">Bari</a> and Rajakhera on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chambal-river">Chambal</a> river.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dholpur was a 15-gun salute state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana-agency">Rajputana Agency</a>, ruled by a Maharaj Rana over a population of farmers in the ravine country of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chambal-river">Chambal</a>. Its red sandstone quarries supplied building stone across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaybhan-singh">Udaybhan Singh</a>, who ruled from 1911, was the last Maharaj Rana.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaybhan-singh">Udaybhan Singh</a> acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and in 1948 Dholpur joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/matsya-union">Matsya Union</a>, which merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan">United State of Rajasthan</a> in 1949. It is now a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dholpur-state.jpg" alt="Dholpur State" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dholpur_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1806 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dholpur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kirat Singh, Udaybhan Singh</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Braj Bhasha, Hindi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dholpur</dd></dl></aside></div>
